        <div class="faq-group">
            <h2 class="faq-group-title">Privacy &amp; how the visit works</h2>
            <details><summary>Will you see my private messages or photos?</summary><p>Only if it is necessary to reduce a specific exposure, always with you present and on your own screen — never opened for review, copied, uploaded, or retained.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Will you take remote access to my device?</summary><p>No. The work is done in person; there is no remote control at any point.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Will anything be uploaded to the cloud?</summary><p>No. Your private data is not sent to any third-party system for processing.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Do you keep logs or copies of my data?</summary><p>No. We keep no log of your digital life. Full-package clients receive a private dated record of the work performed — which is yours, and is not a record of your accounts or messages.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Can the other side tell that changes were made?</summary><p>Sometimes a change is visible by design (for example, ending a session signs that device out). In sensitive situations we plan timing and sequencing with you rather than acting abruptly.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Can my spouse, partner, or business partner tell that I contacted you?</summary><p>Contact is by WhatsApp or Signal and kept minimal. We never reach out to anyone else, and there are no forms or third-party systems involved.</p></details>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-group">
            <h2 class="faq-group-title">Passwords &amp; first contact</h2>
            <details><summary>Do I need to give you my passwords?</summary><p>No. You stay in control of your own credentials throughout.</p></details>
            <details><summary>What should I send in the first message?</summary><p>Just a short, neutral note — for example: &ldquo;I'd like to book a Private Exposure Assessment. The situation is [divorce / business dispute / inheritance / post-incident / other]. Please tell me the next step.&rdquo;</p></details>
            <details><summary>What should I not send?</summary><p>No passwords, screenshots, legal documents, intimate details, recovery codes, or detailed allegations in that first message. Sensitive details are discussed in the right setting, not in chat.</p></details>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-group">
            <h2 class="faq-group-title">Pricing &amp; payment</h2>
            <details><summary>Why does the assessment cost &#8362;3,500?</summary><p>It is a paid, in-person diagnostic with a senior cybersecurity expert — not a sales call. If you continue to a full package within 14 days, it is credited in full.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Is the assessment credited toward a full package?</summary><p>Yes — in full, for any full package booked within 14 days.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Why is Personal Shield &#8362;14,000?</summary><p>It is a full day of in-person expert work for one person and one primary phone, with every account identified together. More people, devices, or complexity are priced on top and scoped before any work begins.</p></details>
            <details><summary>What counts as urgent, and what does it cost?</summary><p>Faster-than-standard scheduling, or emergency handling within 4 hours in Central Israel (a fixed surcharge of &#8362;4,200). If that urgent handling falls on a weekend or holiday, the surcharge is &#8362;5,800 all-in (it replaces the &#8362;4,200, it is not added to it).</p></details>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-group">
            <h2 class="faq-group-title">The assessment &amp; full packages</h2>
            <details><summary>Is the assessment a sales call?</summary><p>No. It is a paid diagnostic. You leave with a clear read on your situation whether or not you book anything further.</p></details>
            <details><summary>What do I actually get from it?</summary><p>A brief, plain-English summary of what was reviewed, what appears most urgent, and what should happen next — including whether a full package is justified and what you should not try to fix alone.</p></details>
            <details><summary>What does Personal Shield include?</summary><p>One person, one day, one primary phone, and every account identified together during the assessment or engagement. &ldquo;Every account&rdquo; means every account we identify together as relevant to your personal digital exposure — not a promise to find accounts you don't surface.</p></details>
            <details><summary>What if I need more than one device or person?</summary><p>Additional devices, additional people, home network, and vehicle reviews are available as add-ons, or — for several people — as Inner Circle Shield. Scope is set before any work begins.</p></details>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-group" id="boundaries">
            <h2 class="faq-group-title">What we never do</h2>
            <details><summary>Can you find out if I was hacked, or who did it?</summary><p>No. We do not investigate or reconstruct the past. We reduce your exposure going forward.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Can you prove who accessed my account?</summary><p>No. That is forensic work, which this service does not do — we focus on reducing your exposure from here on.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Can you investigate my spouse, partner, or business partner?</summary><p>No. We only ever work on your own digital environment, never anyone else's.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Can you collect evidence for court?</summary><p>No. The deliverable is a private record of the work performed — not legal evidence and not a forensic report.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Is this IT support?</summary><p>No. IT support fixes devices. We reduce personal digital exposure when private information, access, or online trails could become leverage.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Is this legal advice?</summary><p>No. We are not a substitute for your attorney, and we do not give legal opinions.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Do you guarantee I'll be safe, or that nothing remains exposed?</summary><p>No honest service can promise that. We reduce the exposure we identify together — and we won't pretend more than that.</p></details>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-group">
            <h2 class="faq-group-title">Attorneys &amp; the private record</h2>
            <details><summary>Can you work with my attorney?</summary><p>Yes, where it helps and only with your permission.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Will I get something my attorney can use?</summary><p>Full-package clients can receive an attorney-friendly summary — a plain-English description of the work performed, provided only if you authorize it. It is not a forensic report, legal opinion, or evidence document.</p></details>
            <details><summary>What is the private dated record? Is it legal evidence?</summary><p>It is a dated record of what was checked and changed during a full package — something tangible you keep. It is not legal certification, a forensic report, court evidence, or a guarantee that no exposure remains.</p></details>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-group">
            <h2 class="faq-group-title">Why not someone you know, and staying safe</h2>
            <details><summary>Why not ask a tech-savvy friend or nephew?</summary><p>This isn't about who can find a setting. It's about judgment, privacy, and discretion in a high-stakes situation. An informal helper can miss the wider picture, make a partial or mistimed change, or learn private things you'd rather they didn't — and turn a serious matter into family knowledge.</p></details>
            <details><summary>What if changing things could make my situation worse?</summary><p>Then timing matters more than speed. In controlling-relationship situations we work to your safety plan and your legal or safety advisor's guidance, and we don't rush access changes that could escalate danger.</p></details>
            <details><summary>What is Annual Shield Review, and can I get it now?</summary><p>It's a yearly review of what changed — new devices, accounts, access, travel, or household arrangements — and a chance to close what should no longer be open. It's offered only after a full package, not after an assessment alone.</p></details>
        </div>
    </div>
